        "original_id": "33426ae3-8285-5b29-8854-dbd15c507fd5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kansas, Kansas City area, Wichita, De Soto High School, Kansas Coliseum\n- Roads: K-10, I-70\n- Media works: The Day After, I Like to Rock\n- Organizations: ABC television network\n\nFacts:\n- On November 11, 1982, the media work \"I Like to Rock\" was recorded at the Kansas Coliseum in Wichita, Kansas.\n- In 1982, several scenes for the television film \"The Day After\" were filmed on K-10 to portray a mass exodus evacuating the Kansas City area on I-70.\n- On November 20, 1983, the television film \"The Day After\" first aired on the ABC television network.\n- During its initial broadcast, \"The Day After\" earned a 46 rating and a 62% audience share.\n- Up to that time, \"The Day After\" was the seventh-highest-rated non-sports show and the highest-rated television film in history.\n- As recently as a 2009 report, \"The Day After\" still held the record as the highest-rated television film in history.\n- K-10 is a 38-mile state highway in Kansas.\n- De Soto High School is located off K-10 and Lexington Avenue on 91st Street.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5a6845db-1870-5f40-947b-21058894ec8d",
        "text": "Page: K-10 (Kansas highway). Sentence: K-10 is a 38-mile (61 km) state highway in the U.S. state of Kansas.\nPage: K-10 (Kansas highway). Sentence: Several scenes for the TV-movie \"The Day After\" were filmed on the highway in 1982 portraying a mass exodus evacuating the Kansas City area on I-70.\nPage: The Day After. Sentence: The Day After is an American television film that first aired on November 20, 1983, on the ABC television network.\nPage: The Day After. Sentence: With a 46 rating and a 62% share of the viewing audience during its initial broadcast, it was the seventh highest rated non-sports show up to that time and set a record as the highest-rated television film in history—a record it still held as recently as a 2009 report.\nPage: De Soto High School (Kansas). Sentence: The school is located off of K-10 and Lexington Avenue on 91st street.\nPage: I Like to Rock. Sentence: It was recorded on November 11, 1982, at the Kansas Coliseum in Wichita, Kansas.",
